  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The waymarked Fenouillet trail starts from Bonporteau beach in Cavalaire-sur-Mer and reaches the Pointe du Dattier. The Fenouillet valley is a cool corner with Mediterranean riverside vegetation, then the trail offers views over the islands, Cap Lardier and the Maures massif. Allow 8 km in 3 h (360 m of elevation gain) for the full route, or 3 km if you come back via the Fenouillet after the first viewpoint (Golfe de Saint-Tropez Destination).</p>
      <p>The land belongs to the Conservatoire du littoral, which presents the Corniche des Maures as a wild area: the Fenouillet trail can be walked freely, without a guide, and the map can be downloaded from the site's page.</p>

      <h2>The possible loops from Bonporteau</h2>
      <p>The commune's 2025 hiking guide describes three routes starting from the same area, east of the hamlet of Le Dattier. The Fenouillet trail alone is a 2.5 km loop of about 1h30, with a cool damp valley then scrubland, rocks and cliffs along the coast. The "old railway line" loop is 5 km, about 2h30: it follows the former Train des Pignes line and goes through the 285 m Dattier tunnel. The small loop around the Foncin estate is 1.5 km in 45 minutes. Durations and distances vary from one source to another, depending on whether several of these routes are combined.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Neither Cavalaire town hall nor the tourist office gives a dog rule for this specific trail. There is only one official reference: in its walking guide, the commune asks you to keep your dog on a leash near flocks (up to 5,500 animals graze in the area) and, when livestock guardian dogs are present, to stop, stay calm and neither threaten nor pet them. A leash is therefore the right option here, especially as the trail is steep and narrow in places.</p>
      <p>In summer, access to the Corniche des Maures massif is regulated from 21 June to 30 September according to the wildfire risk level: a map per massif is published each evening on the Var prefecture website, and access may be banned on days of exceptional risk. It can also be consulted at the tourist office, on the "Golfe de Saint-Tropez" app and via the voice server 04 89 96 43 43. The town guide advises setting out with walking shoes, a cap and water: bring some for your dog too.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: set off early in the morning or late in the day in summer, the ground is cooler under your paws.</div>

      <h2>Access and parking</h2>
      <p>The Fenouillet trail starts from the Maison de la Nature or Bonporteau beach, in the direction of Le Rayol. Park along the RD 559, or in a car park 2 km away on the left, with a start at the far end of the meadow. The Conservatoire's instructions: stay on the waymarked paths, do not smoke or vape, keep a low profile.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Bonporteau underwater trail, steps from the beach, is freely accessible; guided visits with an instructor take place on Tuesdays in July and August. The trail continues beyond the Pointe du Dattier for the more motivated.</p>
